 manpower intensive you have  to have somebody guarding those gaps  24 7 because that's a natural entry  point for folks and so i would urge them  to shore up the gaps where the 18 foot  barrier has  you know if you have 18 foot barrier on  the right and the left you got to close  up that gap otherwise  you're going to be wasting valuable  agent time  to just sit and watch that opening in  the in the wall  um ron how important is it to you as  someone who you know was a former border  patrol chief to see the president or the  vice president for that matter  at the border to go and visit these  facilities  well it means a great deal to the  workforce even at my level when we went  out and visited with  the men and women who were on the front  line and asked them what their needs  were  ask them what their challenges were and  then i could take that back to  washington and work with my staff to try  to meet those needs  um and then there's this whole morale  boost that comes with it you you have  somebody  you know in authority in the government  that that's in your chain of command  including the president that knows what  you do and is eager to  understand it and then provide resources  and provide  uh information and get his staff to plan  to shore up these gaps  to help you know ameliorate this crisis  i think it would be very valuable for  them to do  you know it's not much we know about the  human trafficking part of this  outside of this development this past  week where 90 people were found in a  houston home look like  any home in any idyllic neighborhood in  this country  90 people were crowded in there um what  did you make of it and and the fact that  maybe  what's been happening at the border is  is  is what triggered it well that that's a  symptom you know this is a symptom of  what happens when the border is in chaos  right  these 90 people were smuggled into the  houston area imagine if you lived on  that street  imagine your kids riding their bikes  back and forth along that block  how dangerous that is for for  neighborhoods and then those people 90  people in a small  family home um probably being extorted  probably being human trafficked and if  you've got 90 people who have just  crossed the border illegally there's at  least a handful of them that are there  that have criminal records  um and so it's an unsafe and unsanitary  condition for those individual migrants  to be in but it's also a danger to that  community and it's an example of what  happens  when we don't have sufficient resources  and control at the border  all right now i do know the  administration will tap the agriculture  department to provide  personnel to help i don't know  specifically if it's going to be at the  border iran we just hear  up to 500 individuals i'm i'm not sure  those who  work at the agriculture department ever  signed up for that but what do you what  do you make of it  yeah this was done before in the 2014  surge as well  you're looking for government employees  because they're cleared and they have  known backgrounds so that they could  interact and help alleviate some of the  the uh the shelters or the border patrol  spaces right  so they can do things that help care and  comfort for these migrants that are in  custody  you know rolling back this policy and  not having sufficient resources at the  border  it's going to go down as a mistake it  you know to say that it's getting better  okay fine they've moved more migrants  out of border patrol custody last month  and into hhs care but  not having sufficient shelter space and  reversing the policy without  and knowing that that was going to be  the result um it's just a big mistake  and  unfortunately it's the men and women of  cdp and their families that have to go  through this stress  and they're the ones that are at the  front line that see the bulk of this  problem it's their  they can't say no to this traffic when  an unaccompanied minor comes up to an  immigration officer  whether a cbpo or a border patrol agent  they have to take them into custody  that's the law there's no  there's no option there if there's no  space at hhs that it just continues to  back up  and they've done better but it's nowhere  near to where it needs to be

